    "created_at": "2021-08-09T06:28:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-08-09T06:28:35Z",
    "body": "I have to agree with @woodsp-ibm here. In fact, I would prefer the string-style definitions over any of the previously discussed/proposed designs. I believe it is the most readable out of the lot and it also has the benefits of:\r\n* being easy to be generated programmatically (you could have a mutable list if you wanted but that is easily joined to a string and I don't think this causes a significant overhead in this scenario)\r\n* it is easy read from an input file (if we ever want to move towards that or if a user has a custom script which reads input from a file themselves)\r\n\r\nFurthermore, it also deals with the edge case of an empty side chain natively and is easily extendable towards longer side chains in the future.",
